# Excludelist for `tests/run/` fixtures that the Python backend cannot run.
#
# Intentionally empty: failures from a fresh run should be triaged as backend
# bugs first, not silently exempted. Add an entry only after a fixture has
# been confirmed unsupportable (e.g. requires reflection, JVM-only formatting
# that won't byte-match, threading semantics not modeled in the runtime).
#
# Format: one entry per line, matching the file or directory name as listed
# under `tests/run/`. `#` starts a comment. Always include a `# reason` tag
# so future readers know why the entry was added.
#
# Example:
#   reflect-foo.scala  # uses scala.reflect; not supported by the Python backend

# --- Perf B': hot loops too slow under CPython interpretation -----------
# Triaged 2026-05-02 in `notes/issue-stockrun-timeout-cluster.md`. Each
# of these completes correctly on the JVM and produces correct output
# under the Python backend, but its hot loop exceeds even a 90s harness
# budget. Excluded with reason rather than masked as a flaky timeout.
t8893.scala         # 2 × tick(10000000): 20M tail-recursive iterations
t3502.scala         # LazyList prime sieve up to ~1.4M with per-element % check
collections.scala   # 10 collection types × 5K-iter ++/contains test loops
kmpSliceSearch.scala  # 100×10×5 nested KMP search; dominated by _scpy_is_assignable walks
